  "text": "Information for Veterinarians\nEmergencies\nMenu\nAbout\nAbout the VHC\nFaculty and Staff Directory\nOur Mission\nOur Location\nContact Us\nAcademic Department\nClose\nClients\nClient Information\nMake an Appointment\nFAQs\nClient Billing\nClient Portal\nPay Your Bill Online\nCareCredit\nPharmacy Services\nClient Portal Instructions\nClient Support\nClient Satisfaction Survey\nTouring the VHC\nOur Location\nColumbia Resources: Ways to Refresh While You Wait\nContact Us\nClose\nSmall Animal\nHospital Overview\n573-882-7821\nAfter Hours: 573-882-4589\nDirections\nContact Us\nAnesthesiology\nCardiology\nCommunity Practice\nDentistry\nEmergency and Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology/Neurosurgery\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nSports Medicine and Rehabilitation\nRadiology\nReproduction (Theriogenology)\nShelter Medicine\nSurgery\nCanine Genetics Laboratory\nFeline Genetics and Comparative Medicine Laboratory\nClose\nEquine\nHospital Overview\n573-882-3513\nAfter Hours: 573-882-4589\nDirections\nContact Us\nAmbulatory Service\nAnesthesiology\nInternal Medicine\nLameness Service\nWound Clinic\nOphthalmology\nRadiology\nReproduction (Theriogenology)\nSurgical Services\nClose\nFood Animal\nHospital Overview\n573-882-6857\nAfter Hours: 573-882-4589\nDirections\nContact Us\nHospital Care\nAmbulatory Services\nAnesthesiology\nOphthalmology\nRadiology\nReproduction (Theriogenology)\nClose\nClinical Trials\nReferrals\nReferring Veterinarian Information\nThe Referral Process\nVHC Referral Form\nOvernight Transfers\nVeterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\nRDVM Portal\nReferring Veterinarian Satisfaction Survey\nConsultations\nCardiology Consultation Inquiry\nSmall Animal Internal Medicine Consultation Form\nOrthopedic Referral and Estimate Inquiry\nNeurology Referral Form\nNutrition Referral\nClose\nGiving\nEmployment\nInternal\nYou are here:\nHome\n/\nSmall Animal Hospital\n/\nOncology\n/\nInformation for Veterinarians\nInformation for Veterinarians\nWe gladly accept oncology-related consultation calls for challenging cases that present to your hospital. Our consultation hours are 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. weekdays. These calls are of no cost to you or your client.\nAlthough we strive to take consultation calls as they come in, we can’t guarantee we will always be available. In those cases, our call center will often ask you to provide some information about the case and phone numbers where we can reach you throughout the day or after hours. Our goal is to contact you within 24 hours of your request.\nIf you are referring a patient to us for evaluation, please fax (573-884-0705) or email (\nvmthrefdvm@missouri.edu\n) all pertinent records (bloodwork, biopsy/cytology reports, notes, etc.).\nChemotherapy Patients\nWe look forward to working with you to help us provide excellent care for our chemotherapy patients. We typically require bloodwork (minimum of a CBC) performed no more than 24 hours in advance of a patient receiving chemotherapy. We also require bloodwork to be performed after chemotherapy (dates are determined by chemotherapy treatment protocol). We always ask that a temperature be taken at the same time bloodwork is performed on patients receiving chemotherapy. This information can be critically important to these patients and can help determine if further treatment is indicated. Please complete\nour bloodwork form\nand fax it to 573-884-0705.\nAfter a mutual patient has been seen by the Oncology Service, we will fax or email discharge instructions to you to keep you apprised of the patient’s progress. They will also include information about follow-up instructions we have given to the client and any special tests that may need to be performed until we see the patient again.\nIf you have any questions or concerns about a specific patient and its treatment protocol, do not hesitate to contact our call center at 573-882-7821.\nOncology\nHome\nMeet the Team\nAbout Cancer\nCommon Tumor Types\nCancer Effects\nCommon Cancer Terminology\nCommon Diagnostic Procedures\nCancer Treatment\nSurgery\nChemotherapy\nRadiation Therapy\nClinical Trials\nCurrent Clinical Trials\nTissue Collection Bank\nYour Appointment\nPet-Friendly Lodging\nFlying with Pets\nClient Support\nInformation for Veterinarians\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHow You Can Help\nContact\nSmall Animal Hospital\n573-882-7821; After Hours: 573-882-4589\nRegular hours: M-F, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nEmergencies:\nPlease see current policies\nEquine Hospital\n573-882-3513; After Hours: 573-882-4589\nRegular hours: M-F, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nEmergencies: Open 24 hours a day\nFood Animal Hospital\n573-882-6857; After Hours: 573-882-4589\nRegular hours: M-F, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nEmergencies: Open 24 hours a day\nOur Location\nGiving to the VHC\nThe MU Veterinary Health Center is a leader in animal disease diagnosis,   patient care and education. Individuals and corporations from all over   the world are making a difference every day by providing support for our   facilities, programs,   students and faculty.\nLearn how you can help us continue provide the   most cutting-edge, compassionate care.\n© 2026  — Curators of the\nUniversity of Missouri\n. All rights reserved.\nDMCA\nand\nother copyright information\n.\nAn\nequal opportunity/access/affirmative action/pro-disabled and veteran employer\n.\nDisability Resources",
